  "review_decision": {
    "accepted": true,
    "reason": "The definition correctly narrows the next step to planning metadata from an already accepted ready-only handoff contract. It requires the reviewed handoff-contract surface, ready status, existing handoff metadata, coverage_output_equivalence as a reference policy, and absent command/operator-plan/timing fields before any command argv, estimate-command, efficiency-estimate, or operator-plan metadata may be constructed.",
    "weakest_point": "The accepted boundary includes efficiency_estimate metadata and operator-facing command names, so it is easy to over-read the result as timing evidence, command execution, or native Verilator support. The next implementation must label estimate output as planning metadata only, must not execute generated commands, and must reject closed, malformed, or prepopulated handoff metadata before calling command, estimate, or operator-plan authorities."
  },
